# Copy this file to `.env`, fill in real values there, and NEVER commit `.env`.
# This file (.env.example) carries key NAMES only — no values — and is safe to commit.
# It is the single inventory of secrets for this repo (ruled 2026-10-18); CLAUDE.md and the
# ADRs point here rather than repeating the list.
#
# Where each secret lives:
#   - Locally: `.env` in this repo, for `apify run`, `apify push`, `foundry repair`,
#     `foundry flag` and manual wiki pulls.
#   - Unattended: GitHub Actions repository secrets, each in the smallest set of workflows
#     that needs it:
#       maintainer-check (daily, deterministic): APIFY_TOKEN_SCOPED, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
#       deploy (on the user's merge):            APIFY_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
#       maintainer-repair (not built until the first real escalation, ADR 013):
#                                                CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN, TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID
#       wiki-pull (weekly):                      none — the Store endpoints it reads are public
#       cloud routines (synthesis, target research): none
#     Nowhere else. Never on the Grok Bot computer (shared files and credentials across bots).
#   - The repo hook in .claude/settings.json denies Read and Bash access to `.env*` files by
#     NAME. It is a heuristic and misses indirect reads (dotenv loaders, `source`); it is not
#     the only guard. Side effect: any Bash command whose text mentions `.env` is denied, so
#     edit this file with the Write tool, not a shell heredoc.

# --- Apify ---
APIFY_TOKEN=                 # unscoped account token: apify push (deploy), foundry flag/unflag, local runs
APIFY_TOKEN_SCOPED=          # scoped: read actors and runs, write the actor-foundry-control KV store (daily check only, ADR 012)

# --- Telegram (escalations, repair requests, candidate pings, weekly summary) ---
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=

# --- Claude Code on the runner (repair workflow only, once it exists) ---
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=     # from `claude setup-token` on the existing subscription: no new spend.
                             # An ANTHROPIC_API_KEY route is new recurring spend and needs a ruling.
